From 90aec135b067686dbb29a7035875f3ca67931896 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Intel MPSS <mpss@intel.invalid>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 10:50:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] gas: KNC MVEX encoding and vector operand syntax

From Intel MPSS 3.8.6: build_mvex_prefix emits the 4-byte 0x62 MVEX
prefix (P1 bit 2 clear), operands accept {k1} write masks, register
swizzles ({cdab} ...), memory broadcasts and up/down conversions
({1to16}, {float16}, {uint8} ...), {eh}, and static rounding/SAE
operands ({rn} ... {rz-sae}, {sae}); displacements use the compressed
disp8 of the swizzle/conversion in effect; jknzd/jkzd relax from the
3-byte to the 2-byte VEX form.  Intel syntax gets ZMMWORD PTR.

Intel's L1OM paths are left out.  Vector immediates are only parsed
with .k1omni enabled, so -mnaked-reg no longer turns rn/rd/ru/rz into
immediates in other x86 code.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Anselm Busse <anselm.busse@outlook.com>
